It is Saturday afternoon.
My shift at the café is over.
Now I am relaxing on the sofa.
Tonight my badminton friends Lena and Timo are coming over.
I want to cook something for them.
It should be a typical Berlin meal.
I get my phone and look for a recipe.
One video looks very good.
It is a recipe for Kartoffelsalat with Bouletten.
The chef in the video is very loud and cheerful.
He speaks very directly into the camera.
"Welcome to my Berlin kitchen!" he shouts.
Then he starts immediately with the instructions.
"First, boil the potatoes!" he says loudly.
"Then, cut the onions!"
"Afterwards, mix the meat for the Bouletten!"
I laugh at his energy.
The menu is set, I am cooking that tonight.
